# The ruleset of main requires a code owner's approval (require_code_owner_review, with
# required_approving_review_count 0), so every file named here needs the approval of a member of
# @theorem-labs/engineering, a team of people, and a pull request that touches no file named here
# needs no approval at all. Each line below is a file whose content decides what a person would
# otherwise have to decide, so a change to it cannot be merged on one reading:
#
#   /review.md, /review-change.md,  what the enrollment review and the change review check, and what the
#   /review-issue.md                draft reply to an issue says. .github/workflows/build.yaml reads
#                                   main's copies, so these are the standing instructions to the reviewer.
#   /.claude/skills/write-to-maintainer/  how every message this repository sends an outside maintainer is
#                                   written and judged.
#   /infra/toolchains.tsv           the pinned toolchains every project builds with. This repository has no
#                                   axiom allowlist; this list is the trust list it has.
#   /infra/base-builder/distrust-roots.py  what the build refuses to trust.
#   /.github/CODEOWNERS             this file, which says who owns the files above.
#
# These lines stay the last patterns of the file: the last pattern that matches a file decides its owner.
/review.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/review-change.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/review-issue.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/.claude/skills/write-to-maintainer/ @theorem-labs/engineering
/infra/toolchains.tsv @theorem-labs/engineering
/infra/base-builder/distrust-roots.py @theorem-labs/engineering
/.github/CODEOWNERS @theorem-labs/engineering
